\maketitle*

\begin{abstract}
The \software{hep-cv-private} package adds private CV bibliography filters and environments on top of the HEP CV bibliography setup.
It groups work, visits, education, supervision, funding, talks, publications, software, theses, and service entries by keyword, provides specialised CV bibliography environments for those groups, and formats Indico event and contribution links as eprint data.
\end{abstract}

\tableofcontents\clearpage

\section{Introduction}

Load the package with "\usepackage{hep-cv-private}" after the CV bibliography setup.

\DescribeMacro{work}
\DescribeMacro{visit}
\DescribeMacro{education}
\DescribeMacro{lecture}
\DescribeMacro{tutorial}
\DescribeMacro{master-supervision}
\DescribeMacro{PhD}
\DescribeMacro{master}
\DescribeMacro{funding-individual}
\DescribeMacro{funding-project}
\DescribeMacro{funding-participation}
\DescribeMacro{organization}
The package defines bibliography filters for CV material using keywords in the bibliography database.
The filters cover work, visits, education, lectures, tutorials, master supervision, PhD and master entries, individual, project, and participation funding, and organisation or service entries.

\DescribeMacro{seminar}
\DescribeMacro{conference}
\DescribeMacro{contributions}
\DescribeMacro{student}
Talk-related filters separate invited seminars, invited conferences, contributed conference, workshop, or school presentations, and student presentations.

\DescribeMacro{preprint}
\DescribeMacro{journal}
\DescribeMacro{proceedings}
\DescribeMacro{editor}
\DescribeMacro{community}
\DescribeMacro{software}
\DescribeMacro{thesis}
\DescribeMacro{main}
Publication filters group preprints, journal articles, proceedings, editor entries, community entries, software, theses, and selected main-recent publications.

\DescribeEnv{work}
\DescribeEnv{visit}
\DescribeEnv{education}
\DescribeEnv{student}
\DescribeEnv{course}
\DescribeEnv{funding}
\DescribeEnv{talk}
\DescribeEnv{publication}
\DescribeEnv{main}
The corresponding bibliography environments customise the CV left-column layout and field formatting for positions, visits, education, students, courses, funding, talks, publications, and selected main publications.
They move titles, dates, event information, funding titles, annotations, or presentation styles to the positions expected in a private CV.

\DescribeMacro{CERN}
\DescribeMacro{INFN}
\DescribeMacro{IJS}
\DescribeMacro{DESY}
\DescribeMacro{FNAL}
\DescribeMacro{Edinburgh}
\DescribeMacro{CNRS}
\DescribeMacro{IIHE}
\DescribeMacro{IRMP}
\DescribeMacro{MITP}
\DescribeMacro{LIP}
The package also defines Indico eprint formats for common event servers.
Entries can use these eprint types to link both the event and a contribution number.

